When `subFieldIndex` is `FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD`, which is the common case, the rewrite skips `CanSupportSubField`. That avoids a second `GetField` lookup, which scans the field list a second time.

This rests on an assumption I have not checked against the source of `CanSupportSubField`. The skip is only safe if that function always returns true for the main-field index once the field exists. All other `subFieldIndex` values still go through the original check.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Mesg::GetFieldUINT8Value(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum, const FIT_UINT8 fieldArrayIndex, const FIT_UINT16 subFieldIndex) const
{
    const Field *field = GetField(fieldNum);

    if (field == FIT_NULL)
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    if ((subFieldIndex != FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD) && (!CanSupportSubField(fieldNum, subFieldIndex)))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return field->GetUINT8Value(fieldArrayIndex);
}
```